Optimal Solution - Dynamic programming solution to compute edit distance using insert, delete, and replace operations.
                   Define DP on string prefixes and choose the cheapest operation at each mismatch.

class Solution {
    public int minDistance(String word1, String word2) {
        // Lengths of the two words
        final int m = word1.length();
        final int n = word2.length();
        // DP table where costDp[i][j] represents
        // minimum operations to convert word1[0..i-1] to word2[0..j-1]
        int[][] costDp = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        // Base case: converting word1[0..i-1] to empty string (all deletions)
        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++)
            costDp[i][0] = i;
        // Base case: converting empty string to word2[0..j-1] (all insertions)
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)
            costDp[0][i] = i;
        // Fill the DP table
        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                // If characters match, no operation needed
                if (word1.charAt(i - 1) == word2.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    costDp[i][j] = costDp[i - 1][j - 1];
                }
                // Otherwise, choose the minimum of replace, delete, or insert
                else {
                    int topLeft = costDp[i - 1][j - 1]; // replace
                    int top = costDp[i - 1][j];         // delete
                    int left = costDp[i][j - 1];        // insert
                    costDp[i][j] = Math.min(topLeft, Math.min(top, left)) + 1;
                }
            }
        }
        // Final answer: minimum edit distance
        return costDp[m][n];
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(m * n).
Space Complexity :- O(m * n).
